      "rev_n_10_29e724_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_29e724_1",
        "node_id": "n_10_29e724",
        "thought_text": "Calculate the expected value directly using the formula for the expected maximum of a set of independent and identically distributed random variables. For a fair die with \\( m \\) faces, the expected value of a single roll is \\( E(X) = \\frac{m+1}{2} \\). The expected maximum of \\( n \\) such rolls can be approximated using the formula \\( E(\\text{Max}(X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_n)) \\approx \\frac{m+1}{2} \\left(1 - \\left(1 - \\frac{2}{m}\\right)^n\\right) \\). This approach avoids the need for simulation and provides a more accurate and efficient solution.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-11327197880840935",
